
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
AB = BC [00]
AB ⟂ BC [01]
AB ∥ CD [02]
AD ∥ BC [03]
BE = BC [04]
B,D,E are collinear [05]
D,C,F are collinear [06]
EF ⟂ BD [07]
DF:BD = DF:BD [08]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. AB = BC [00] & BE = BC [04] ⇒  B is the circumcenter of \Delta ACE [09]
002. B,D,E are collinear [05] & BD ⟂ EF [07] ⇒  BE ⟂ EF [10]
003. B is the circumcenter of \Delta ACE [09] & BE ⟂ EF [10] ⇒  ∠CEF = ∠CAE [11]
004. AB ⟂ BC [01] & AB ∥ CD [02] ⇒  BC ⟂ CD [12]
005. B is the circumcenter of \Delta ACE [09] & BC ⟂ CD [12] ⇒  ∠DCE = ∠CAE [13]
006. F,C,D are collinear [06] & ∠CEF = ∠CAE [11] & ∠DCE = ∠CAE [13] & AB ∥ CD [02] ⇒  ∠FCE = ∠CEF [14]
007. ∠FCE = ∠CEF [14] ⇒  FC = FE [15]
008. B,D,E are collinear [05] & EF ⟂ BD [07] & AB ⟂ BC [01] & AB ∥ CD [02] ⇒  ∠BCD = ∠DEF [16]
009. B,D,E are collinear [05] & D,C,F are collinear [06] ⇒  ∠BDC = ∠EDF [17]
010. ∠BCD = ∠DEF [16] & ∠BDC = ∠EDF [17] (Similar Triangles)⇒  DC:BD = DE:DF [18]
011. ∠BCD = ∠DEF [16] & ∠BDC = ∠EDF [17] (Similar Triangles)⇒  BC:BD = FE:FD [19]
012. BC ∥ AD [03] & AB ∥ CD [02] ⇒  ∠ADC = ∠CBA [20]
013. CD ∥ AB [02] ⇒  ∠ACD = ∠CAB [21]
014. ∠ADC = ∠CBA [20] & ∠ACD = ∠CAB [21] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CD = AB [22]
015. DC:BD = DE:DF [18] & BC:BD = FE:FD [19] & CD = AB [22] & AB = BC [00] ⇒  FE:DF = DE:DF [23]
016. FE:DF = DE:DF [23] & DF:BD = DF:BD [08] ⇒  FE = DE [24]
017. FC = FE [15] & FE = DE [24] ⇒  ED = CF
